        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles A. Agemian, Arshile Gorky\n- Companies: Chase Manhattan Bank, Hackensack Trust Co., Garden State National Bank\n- Roles: banker, executive vice president of operations, chairman, chief executive officer, painter\n- Concepts: Abstract Expressionism\n\nFacts:\n- Arshile Gorky was born as Vostanik Manoug Adoian on April 15, 1904, and he became an Armenian-American painter.\n- Charles A. Agemian was born on July 22, 1909, and he became an American banker.\n- Arshile Gorky had a seminal influence on Abstract Expressionism.\n- Arshile Gorky died on July 21, 1948.\n- Charles A. Agemian took early retirement from Chase Manhattan Bank, where he had served as executive vice president of operations.\n- Charles A. Agemian became chairman and chief executive officer of Hackensack Trust Co.\n- Hackensack Trust Co. was later renamed Garden State National Bank.\n- Charles A. Agemian died on March 30, 1996.",
